{"items":[{"id":"cap-v2-ordering_and_selection-rust-generation-01","problem":"Implement a deterministic consolidation API in `solution.rs` using only the Rust standard library. Do not include a `main` function.

Expose exactly these public declarations:

```rust
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct Reading {
    pub sensor: String,
    pub quality: i32,
    pub arrival: u32,
    pub value: String,
}

pub fn consolidate_readings(readings: &[Reading]) -> Vec<Reading>;
```

A sensor may occur more than once. Retain exactly one reading per distinct `sensor`. A duplicate replaces the current winner when it has higher `quality`; if qualities tie, prefer the smaller `arrival`; if both tie, prefer the lexicographically smaller `value`.

Return the retained readings ordered by decreasing `quality`, then increasing `arrival`, then lexicographically increasing `sensor`, and finally lexicographically increasing `value`. The input slice must not be modified. Empty input returns an empty vector.","reference_code":"use std::collections::HashMap;

#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct Reading {
    pub sensor: String,
    pub quality: i32,
    pub arrival: u32,
    pub value: String,
}

pub fn consolidate_readings(readings: &[Reading]) -> Vec<Reading> {
    let mut winners: HashMap<String, Reading> = HashMap::new();

    for reading in readings {
        match winners.get(&reading.sensor) {
            None => {
                winners.insert(reading.sensor.clone(), reading.clone());
            }
            Some(current) => {
                let is_better = reading.quality > current.quality
                    || (reading.quality == current.quality
                        && (reading.arrival < current.arrival
                            || (reading.arrival == current.arrival
                                && reading.value < current.value)));
                if is_better {
                    winners.insert(reading.sensor.clone(), reading.clone());
                }
            }
        }
    }

    let mut result: Vec<Reading> = winners.into_values().collect();
    result.sort_by(|a, b| {
        b.quality
            .cmp(&a.quality)
            .then_with(|| a.arrival.cmp(&b.arrival))
            .then_with(|| a.sensor.cmp(&b.sensor))
            .then_with(|| a.value.cmp(&b.value))
    });
    result
}
