An entrant may have multiple entries. Before applying `limit`, retain the entrant's highest-scoring entry. For equal scores, prefer the smaller attempt number; if those also tie, prefer the lexicographically smaller division.

Rank the retained entries by decreasing score, increasing attempt number, lexicographically increasing entrant, then lexicographically increasing division. Return at most `limit` entries in that order. Thus duplicate submissions never consume multiple finalist positions. A zero limit or empty input returns an empty vector. Do not mutate the input.","reference_code":"use std::collections::HashSet;

